// REJECTS: Service mcpServer should be a valid identifier ([a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z0-9_]*)
//
// Same shape as the execution-param key, different element: `mcpServer:` takes an
// `identifier`, quoted strings are identifiers, and the walker then applies a regex the
// grammar knows nothing about. 'not-a-valid-identifier' is a legal STRING and an illegal
// mcpServer name.
###Service
Service fixture::neg::BadMcpServerName
{
   pattern: '/x';
   documentation: 'd';
   mcpServer: 'not-a-valid-identifier';
   execution: Single
   {
      query: |fixture::neg::Person.all();
      mapping: fixture::neg::M;
      runtime: fixture::neg::R;
   }
}
